'''''Lonicera'' × ''heckrottii''''', the '''golden flame honeysuckle''', is a [[plant]] in the honeysuckle family, [[Caprifoliaceae]], grown in [[garden]]s for its showy flowers and long season of bloom.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|title=Lonicera × heckrottii 'Gold Flame' - Plant Finder|url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?kempercode=b839|access-date=2020-12-12|website=www.missouribotanicalgarden.org}}</ref>

==Description==
''Lonicera'' × ''heckrottii'' is a [[vine]] with opposite, simple [[leaf|leaves]], on twining stems. They have fragrant pink to yellow flowers.<ref name=":0" /> ''Lonicera x heckrotti'' is believed to be a hybrid of ''[[Lonicera sempervirens]]'' and ''Lonicera x americana''.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lonicera x heckrottii (Everblooming Honeysuckle, Goldflame Honeysuckle) {{!}} North Carolina Extension Gardener Plant Toolbox|url=https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/lonicera-x-heckrottii/|access-date=2020-12-12|website=plants.ces.ncsu.edu}}</ref>

